{"strongs": "H1116", "word": "בָּמָה", "translit": "ba.mah", "root": "במה", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "high place", "definition": "בָּמָה 104 noun feminine high place (√ apparently בום on account of firm ָ֯ ; compare Assyrian bâmâtê Zim BP 48, Moab. במת MI 3, 27 ) — Jer 48:35 + 18 t.; הַבָּמָ֫תָה 1Sam 9:13 plural בָּמוֺת Num 21:19 + 62 t.; construct בָּֽמֳתֵי Job 9:8 ; Isa 14:14 ; Amos 4:13 בָּֽמֳו֯תֵי Deut 32:13 ; Isa 58:14 ; Mic 1:3 ( Ew § 211 d Ges «GKC:87»§ 87 , 5 archaic feminine construct with retracted accent before monosyl. in poetry, bâm©-thê not b©m ); suffix בָּמֹתַי 2Sam 22:34 + 3 t.; בָּמוֺתַי Ps 18:34 + 10 t.; — 1. high place, mountain: בָּמוֺת יָעַר forest mountains Mic 3:12 = Jer 26:18 במות עולם ancient mountains Ezek 36:2 במות ארנן Num 21:28 ( E poetry) 2. high places, battle-fields , the chief places of the land giving possession, victory, dominion: על במותיך on thy high places (Gilboa, the battle-field) 2Sam 1:19 ; 2Sam 1:25 (in v 2Sam 1:19 ᵐ5 has a doublet מֵתֶיךָ thy dead , see We Dr ). \\ \\ a. of Israel: רכב על במתי ארץ ride upon the high places of the land Deut 32:13 & Isa 58:14 compare Deut 33:29 ; Ps 18:34 = 2Sam 22:34 ; Hab 3:19 . \\ \\ b. of God: דרך על במתי ארץ tread upon the high places of the earth Amos 4:13 compare Mic 1:3 במתי ים Job 9:8 עלה על במתי עב (aspiration of the king of Babylon) Isa 14:14 . 3. high places , as places of worship, at first on hills and mountains, later on artificial mounds or platforms, under green trees, and in cities; still later for the chapels erected thereon, and once apparently for a portable sanctuary (decked with diverse colours) Ezek 16:16 . The ancient worship of Israel was conducted on these high places. In the times of Samuel and David they ascended to them, descended from them, and offered sacrifices on them, 1Sam 9:12-25 ; 1Sam 10:5 ; 1Sam 10:13 ( הבמה for הביתה We Dr ). The custom continued in the reign of Solomon, but Gibeon was הבמה הגדולה 1Kgs 3:2-4 compare 1Chr 16:39 ; 1Chr 21:29 ; 2Chr 1:3 ; 2Chr 1:13 . High places of Baal were also used Num 22:41 ( E ) Jer 19:5 ; Jer 32:35 of Moab Isa 15:2 ; Isa 16:12 ; Jer 48:35 (compare MI 27 ); these must be demolished Num 33:52 ( J ). Solomon built במות (platforms or chapels) to Chemosh and Milkom on the Mt. of Evil Counsel opposite Jerusalem 1Kgs 11:7 : Jeroboam made temples on the ancient high places of Dan and Bethel 1Kgs 12:31 ; 1Kgs 12:32 ; 2Chr 11:15 they are called במות און Hos 10:8 , במות ישׂחק Amos 7:9 : the kings of Israel built במות and בתי הבמות in all their cities 2Kgs 17:9 , and the people worshipped there 2Kgs 17:11 these were also used by the mixed population after the exile of Israel 2Kgs 17:29 ; 2Kgs 17:32 (twice in verse): these various idolatrous high places were first destroyed by Josiah 1Kgs 13:2 ; 1Kgs 13:32 ; 1Kgs 13:38 ; 2Kgs 23:5-20 ; 2Chr 34:3 . The worship of Yahweh on high places continued in Judah until the exile 1Kgs 22:44 ; 2Kgs 15:35 the sanctity code predicts that Yahweh will destroy them Lev 26:30 they were regarded as the reason for the rejection of Shiloh Ps 78:58 . The compiler of Kings, writing from the point of view of the Deuteronomic code, complains רַק הַבָּמוֺת לֹא סָרוּ 2Kgs 12:4 ; 2Kgs 14:4 ; 2Kgs 15:4 ; 2Kgs 15:35 compare 2Chr 15:17 ; 2Chr 20:33 , and praises the few pious kings who destroyed them. \\ \\ a. Rehoboam built במות with מצבות & אשׁרים on every high hill and under every green tree 1Kgs 14:23 . \\ \\ b. Asa did not remove the high places 1Kgs 15:14 ( 2Chr 14:2 ; 2Chr 14:4 is incorrect unless במות בעל ). \\ \\ c. Jehoshaphat in his reform on the basis of the covenant code did not remove them 1Kgs 22:44 ( עוֺד הֵסִיר אֶתהַֿבָּמוֺת 2Chr 17:16 is doubtless incorrect, possibly read מצבות ); Jehoram, his son, made high places in the cities of Judah 2Chr 21:11 ( ᵐ5 ᵑ9 ; not mountains HCT); and Ahaz sacrificed on high places on the hills and under every green tree and in every city of Judah 2Kgs 16:4 ; 2Chr 28:4 ; 2Chr 28:25 compare Mic 1:5 (read חטאת ? so ᵐ5 ᵑ6 ᵑ7 Che and others; yet compare JBL 1890, 73 f. ) \\ \\ d. Hezekiah removed them 2Kgs 18:4 ; 2Kgs 18:22 ; 2Chr 31:1 ; 2Chr 32:12 ; Isa 36:7 but Manasseh rebuilt them 2Kgs 21:3 ; 2Chr 33:3 ; 2Chr 33:19 , and the people continued to sacrifice thereon to Yahweh 2Chr 33:17 . \\ \\ e. Josiah, in his reform, based on the Deuteronomic code, defiled them and brake them down from Geba to Beersheba 2Kgs 23:5 ; 2Kgs 23:8 ; 2Kgs 23:9 but subsequently there were במות התפת in the valley of Ben Hinnom Jer 7:31 , and במות throughout Judah Jer 17:3 compare Ezek 6:3 ; Ezek 6:6 ; Ezek 20:29 (questioned by Ew & Co ). 4. funereal mound (?) Ezek 43:7 ( Thes , but in their high places AV RV ; in their death ᵑ7 Theod Ew Hi RVm ), Isa 53:9 (Lowth Ew Bö Rodwell Orelli ; but in his death AV RV , or martyr death De Che Br ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1157')\">BDB1157</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H1116')\">H1116</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1156')\">BDB1156</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1158')\">BDB1158</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>בָּמָה</bdbheb><sub>104</sub> <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>high place</highlightword> (√ apparently <bdbheb>בום</bdbheb> on account of firm <bdbheb>ָ֯</bdbheb>; compare Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>bâmâtê</highlight></transliteration> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Zim')\">Zim<sup>BP 48, Moab.</sup></lookup> <bdbheb>במת</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('MI')\"><reflink>MI</reflink><sup>3, 27</sup></lookup>) — <ref ref=\"Jer 48:35\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"35\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"35\" onclick=\"bcv(24,48,35)\">Jer 48:35</ref> + 18 t.; <bdbheb>הַבָּמָ֫תָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Sam 9:13\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(9,9,13)\">1Sam 9:13</ref> plural <bdbheb>בָּמוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 21:19\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(4,21,19)\">Num 21:19</ref> + 62 t.; construct <bdbheb>בָּֽמֳתֵי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 9:8\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(18,9,8)\">Job 9:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 14:14\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(23,14,14)\">Isa 14:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Amos 4:13\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(30,4,13)\">Amos 4:13</ref> <bdbheb>בָּֽמֳו֯תֵי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 32:13\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(5,32,13)\">Deut 32:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 58:14\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"58\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"58\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(23,58,14)\">Isa 58:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Mic 1:3\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(33,1,3)\">Mic 1:3</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew<sup>§ 211 d</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup><sup>«GKC:87»§ 87</sup>, 5 archaic feminine construct with retracted accent before monosyl. in poetry, <transliteration><highlight>bâm©-thê</highlight></transliteration> not <transliteration><highlight>b©m</highlight></transliteration>); suffix <bdbheb>בָּמֹתַי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Sam 22:34\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(10,22,34)\">2Sam 22:34</ref> + 3 t.; <bdbheb>בָּמוֺתַי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 18:34\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(19,18,34)\">Ps 18:34</ref> + 10 t.; — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>high place, mountain:</highlight> <bdbheb>בָּמוֺת יָעַר</bdbheb> <highlight>forest mountains</highlight> <ref ref=\"Mic 3:12\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(33,3,12)\">Mic 3:12</ref> = <ref ref=\"Jer 26:18\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(24,26,18)\">Jer 26:18</ref> <bdbheb>במות עולם</bdbheb> <highlight>ancient mountains</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ezek 36:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"36\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"36\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,36,2)\">Ezek 36:2</ref> <bdbheb>במות ארנן</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 21:28\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(4,21,28)\">Num 21:28</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup> poetry) </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> <highlight>high places, battle-fields</highlight>, the chief places of the land giving possession, victory, dominion: <bdbheb>על במותיך</bdbheb> <highlight>on thy high places</highlight> (Gilboa, the battle-field) <ref ref=\"2Sam 1:19\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(10,1,19)\">2Sam 1:19</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 1:25\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(10,1,25)\">2Sam 1:25</ref> (in v<ref ref=\"2Sam 1:19\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(10,1,19)\">2Sam 1:19</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> has a doublet <bdbheb>מֵתֶיךָ</bdbheb> <highlight>thy dead</highlight>, see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('We')\">We</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dr')\">Dr</lookup>). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> <highlight>of Israel:</highlight> <bdbheb>רכב על במתי</bdbheb> <bdbheb>ארץ</bdbheb> <highlight>ride upon the high places of the land</highlight> <ref ref=\"Deut 32:13\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(5,32,13)\">Deut 32:13</ref> &amp; <ref ref=\"Isa 58:14\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"58\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"58\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(23,58,14)\">Isa 58:14</ref> compare <ref ref=\"Deut 33:29\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(5,33,29)\">Deut 33:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 18:34\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(19,18,34)\">Ps 18:34</ref> = <ref ref=\"2Sam 22:34\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(10,22,34)\">2Sam 22:34</ref>; <ref ref=\"Hab 3:19\" b=\"35\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(35,3,19)\">Hab 3:19</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> <highlight>of God:</highlight> <bdbheb>דרך על במתי ארץ</bdbheb> <highlight>tread upon the high places of the earth</highlight> <ref ref=\"Amos 4:13\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(30,4,13)\">Amos 4:13</ref> compare <ref ref=\"Mic 1:3\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(33,1,3)\">Mic 1:3</ref> <bdbheb>במתי ים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 9:8\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(18,9,8)\">Job 9:8</ref> <bdbheb>עלה על במתי עב</bdbheb> (aspiration of the king of Babylon) <ref ref=\"Isa 14:14\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(23,14,14)\">Isa 14:14</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>3.</b> <highlight>high places</highlight>, as places of worship, at first on hills and mountains, later on artificial mounds or platforms, under green trees, and in cities; still later for the chapels erected thereon, and once apparently for a portable sanctuary (decked with diverse colours) <ref ref=\"Ezek 16:16\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(26,16,16)\">Ezek 16:16</ref>. The ancient worship of Israel was conducted on these high places. In the times of Samuel and David they ascended to them, descended from them, and offered sacrifices on them, <ref ref=\"1Sam 9:12-25\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(9,9,12)\">1Sam 9:12-25</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 10:5\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(9,10,5)\">1Sam 10:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Sam 10:13\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(9,10,13)\">1Sam 10:13</ref> (<bdbheb>הבמה</bdbheb> for <bdbheb>הביתה</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('We')\">We</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dr')\">Dr</lookup>). The custom continued in the reign of Solomon, but Gibeon was <bdbheb>הבמה</bdbheb> <bdbheb>הגדולה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 3:2-4\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(11,3,2)\">1Kgs 3:2-4</ref> compare <ref ref=\"1Chr 16:39\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"39\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"39\" onclick=\"bcv(13,16,39)\">1Chr 16:39</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Chr 21:29\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(13,21,29)\">1Chr 21:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 1:3\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(14,1,3)\">2Chr 1:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 1:13\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(14,1,13)\">2Chr 1:13</ref>. High places of Baal were also used <ref ref=\"Num 22:41\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"41\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"41\" onclick=\"bcv(4,22,41)\">Num 22:41</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>) <ref ref=\"Jer 19:5\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(24,19,5)\">Jer 19:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 32:35\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"35\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"35\" onclick=\"bcv(24,32,35)\">Jer 32:35</ref> of Moab <ref ref=\"Isa 15:2\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(23,15,2)\">Isa 15:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 16:12\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(23,16,12)\">Isa 16:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 48:35\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"35\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"35\" onclick=\"bcv(24,48,35)\">Jer 48:35</ref> (compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('MI')\"><reflink>MI</reflink><sup>27</sup></lookup>); these must be demolished <ref ref=\"Num 33:52\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"52\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"52\" onclick=\"bcv(4,33,52)\">Num 33:52</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>). Solomon built <bdbheb>במות</bdbheb> (platforms or chapels) to Chemosh and Milkom on the Mt. of Evil Counsel opposite Jerusalem <ref ref=\"1Kgs 11:7\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(11,11,7)\">1Kgs 11:7</ref>: Jeroboam made temples on the ancient high places of Dan and Bethel <ref ref=\"1Kgs 12:31\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(11,12,31)\">1Kgs 12:31</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 12:32\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"32\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"32\" onclick=\"bcv(11,12,32)\">1Kgs 12:32</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 11:15\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(14,11,15)\">2Chr 11:15</ref> they are called <bdbheb>במות און</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Hos 10:8\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(28,10,8)\">Hos 10:8</ref>, <bdbheb>במות ישׂחק</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Amos 7:9\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(30,7,9)\">Amos 7:9</ref>: the kings of Israel built <bdbheb>במות</bdbheb> and <bdbheb>בתי הבמות</bdbheb> in all their cities <ref ref=\"2Kgs 17:9\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(12,17,9)\">2Kgs 17:9</ref>, and the people worshipped there <ref ref=\"2Kgs 17:11\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(12,17,11)\">2Kgs 17:11</ref> these were also used by the mixed population after the exile of Israel <ref ref=\"2Kgs 17:29\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(12,17,29)\">2Kgs 17:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 17:32\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"32\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"32\" onclick=\"bcv(12,17,32)\">2Kgs 17:32</ref> (twice in verse): these various idolatrous high places were first destroyed by Josiah <ref ref=\"1Kgs 13:2\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(11,13,2)\">1Kgs 13:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 13:32\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"32\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"32\" onclick=\"bcv(11,13,32)\">1Kgs 13:32</ref>; <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"1Kgs 13:38\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"38\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"38\" onclick=\"bcv(11,13,38)\">1Kgs 13:38</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 23:5-20\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(12,23,5)\">2Kgs 23:5-20</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 34:3\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(14,34,3)\">2Chr 34:3</ref>. The worship of Yahweh on high places continued in Judah until the exile <ref ref=\"1Kgs 22:44\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"44\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"44\" onclick=\"bcv(11,22,44)\">1Kgs 22:44</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 15:35\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"35\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"35\" onclick=\"bcv(12,15,35)\">2Kgs 15:35</ref> the sanctity code predicts that Yahweh will destroy them <ref ref=\"Lev 26:30\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(3,26,30)\">Lev 26:30</ref> they were regarded as the reason for the rejection of Shiloh <ref ref=\"Ps 78:58\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"78\" vBegin=\"58\" cEnd=\"78\" vEnd=\"58\" onclick=\"bcv(19,78,58)\">Ps 78:58</ref>. The compiler of Kings, writing from the point of view of the Deuteronomic code, complains <bdbheb>רַק הַבָּמוֺת</bdbheb> <bdbheb>לֹא סָרוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Kgs 12:4\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(12,12,4)\">2Kgs 12:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 14:4\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(12,14,4)\">2Kgs 14:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 15:4\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(12,15,4)\">2Kgs 15:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 15:35\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"35\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"35\" onclick=\"bcv(12,15,35)\">2Kgs 15:35</ref> compare <ref ref=\"2Chr 15:17\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(14,15,17)\">2Chr 15:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 20:33\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"33\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"33\" onclick=\"bcv(14,20,33)\">2Chr 20:33</ref>, and praises the few pious kings who destroyed them. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> Rehoboam built <bdbheb>במות</bdbheb> with <bdbheb>מצבות</bdbheb> &amp; <bdbheb>אשׁרים</bdbheb> on every high hill and under every green tree <ref ref=\"1Kgs 14:23\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(11,14,23)\">1Kgs 14:23</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> Asa did not remove the high places <ref ref=\"1Kgs 15:14\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(11,15,14)\">1Kgs 15:14</ref> (<ref ref=\"2Chr 14:2\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(14,14,2)\">2Chr 14:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 14:4\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(14,14,4)\">2Chr 14:4</ref> is incorrect unless <bdbheb>במות בעל</bdbheb>). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>c.</b> Jehoshaphat in his reform on the basis of the covenant code did not remove them <ref ref=\"1Kgs 22:44\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"44\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"44\" onclick=\"bcv(11,22,44)\">1Kgs 22:44</ref> (<bdbheb>עוֺד הֵסִיר אֶתהַֿבָּמוֺת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Chr 17:16\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(14,17,16)\">2Chr 17:16</ref> is doubtless incorrect, possibly read <bdbheb>מצבות</bdbheb>); Jehoram, his son, made high places in the cities of Judah <ref ref=\"2Chr 21:11\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(14,21,11)\">2Chr 21:11</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ9</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>; not <highlight>mountains</highlight> HCT); and Ahaz sacrificed on high places on the hills and under every green tree and in every city of Judah <ref ref=\"2Kgs 16:4\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(12,16,4)\">2Kgs 16:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 28:4\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(14,28,4)\">2Chr 28:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 28:25\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(14,28,25)\">2Chr 28:25</ref> compare <ref ref=\"Mic 1:5\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(33,1,5)\">Mic 1:5</ref> (read <bdbheb>חטאת</bdbheb>? so <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Syr')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ6</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Che')\">Che</lookup> and others; yet compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('JBL')\">JBL<sup>1890, 73 f.</sup></lookup>) <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>d.</b> Hezekiah removed them <ref ref=\"2Kgs 18:4\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(12,18,4)\">2Kgs 18:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 18:22\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(12,18,22)\">2Kgs 18:22</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 31:1\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(14,31,1)\">2Chr 31:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 32:12\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(14,32,12)\">2Chr 32:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 36:7\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"36\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"36\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(23,36,7)\">Isa 36:7</ref> but Manasseh rebuilt them <ref ref=\"2Kgs 21:3\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(12,21,3)\">2Kgs 21:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 33:3\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(14,33,3)\">2Chr 33:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Chr 33:19\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(14,33,19)\">2Chr 33:19</ref>, and the people continued to sacrifice thereon to Yahweh <ref ref=\"2Chr 33:17\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(14,33,17)\">2Chr 33:17</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>e.</b> Josiah, in his reform, based on the Deuteronomic code, defiled them and brake them down from Geba to Beersheba <ref ref=\"2Kgs 23:5\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(12,23,5)\">2Kgs 23:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 23:8\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(12,23,8)\">2Kgs 23:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 23:9\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(12,23,9)\">2Kgs 23:9</ref> but subsequently there were <bdbheb>במות</bdbheb> <bdbheb>התפת</bdbheb> in the valley of Ben Hinnom <ref ref=\"Jer 7:31\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(24,7,31)\">Jer 7:31</ref>, and <bdbheb>במות</bdbheb> throughout Judah <ref ref=\"Jer 17:3\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(24,17,3)\">Jer 17:3</ref> compare <ref ref=\"Ezek 6:3\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(26,6,3)\">Ezek 6:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 6:6\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(26,6,6)\">Ezek 6:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 20:29\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(26,20,29)\">Ezek 20:29</ref> (questioned by <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> &amp; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Co')\">Co</lookup>). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>4.</b> <highlight>funereal mound</highlight> (?) <ref ref=\"Ezek 43:7\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"43\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"43\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(26,43,7)\">Ezek 43:7</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Thes')\">Thes</lookup>, but <highlight>in their high places</highlight> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('AV')\"><reflink>AV</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('RV')\"><reflink>RV</reflink></lookup>; <highlight>in their death</highlight> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Theod')\"><reflink>Theod</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hi')\">Hi</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('RV')\"><reflink>RVm</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Isa 53:9\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"53\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"53\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(23,53,9)\">Isa 53:9</ref> (Lowth <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Bö')\">Bö</lookup> Rodwell <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Or')\">Orelli</lookup>; but <highlight>in his death</highlight> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('AV')\"><reflink>AV</reflink></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('RV')\"><reflink>RV</reflink></lookup>, or <highlight>martyr death</highlight> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('De')\">De</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Che')\">Che</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Br')\">Br</lookup>). </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Jer 48:35", "book": "JER", "chapter": 48, "verse": 35}, {"raw": "1Sam 9:13", "book": "1SA", "chapter": 9, "verse": 13}, {"raw": "Num 21:19", "book": "NUM", "chapter": 21, "verse": 19}, {"raw": "Job 9:8", "book": "JOB", "chapter": 9, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Isa 14:14", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 14, "verse": 14}, {"raw": "Amos 4:13", "book": "AMO", "chapter": 4, "verse": 13}, {"raw": "Deut 32:13", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 32, "verse": 13}, {"raw": "Isa 58:14", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 58, "verse": 14}, {"raw": "Mic 1:3", "book": "MIC", "chapter": 1, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "2Sam 22:34", "book": "2SA", "chapter": 22, "verse": 34}, {"raw": "Ps 18:34", "book": "PSA", "chapter": 18, "verse": 34}, {"raw": "Mic 3:12", "book": "MIC", "chapter": 3, "verse": 12}, {"raw": "Jer 26:18", "book": "JER", "chapter": 26, "verse": 18}, {"raw": "Ezek 36:2", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 36, "verse": 2}, {"raw": "Num 21:28", "book": "NUM", "chapter": 21, "verse": 28}, {"raw": "2Sam 1:19", "book": "2SA", "chapter": 1, "verse": 19}, {"raw": "2Sam 1:25", "book": "2SA", "chapter": 1, "verse": 25}, {"raw": "Deut 33:29", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 33, "verse": 29}, {"raw": "Hab 3:19", "book": "HAB", "chapter": 3, "verse": 19}